   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "outlier_detection_sec11",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 11. Outlier Detection\n",
    "We apply the standard **Interquartile Range (IQR)** method on experimental measurement errors to detect statistical anomalies without deleting observations.\n",
    "\n",
    "### IQR Formulation\n",
    "- $Q_1 = \\text{25th percentile}$\n",
    "- $Q_3 = \\text{75th percentile}$\n",
    "- $\\text{IQR} = Q_3 - Q_1$\n",
    "- $\\text{Lower Bound} = Q_1 - 1.5 \\times \\text{IQR}$\n",
    "- $\\text{Upper Bound} = Q_3 + 1.5 \\times \\text{IQR}$\n",
    "\n",
    "*Note: Outliers represent important physical variations (such as stopwatch pressing offsets) and are flagged with `Outlier_Flag` rather than deleted.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "outlier_detection_code",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Pre-calculate Percentage_Error for outlier analysis\n",
    "df_preprocessed['Error_s'] = (df_preprocessed['Experimental_Period_s'] - df_preprocessed['Theoretical_Period_s']).round(4)\n",
    "df_preprocessed['Absolute_Error_s'] = df_preprocessed['Error_s'].abs().round(4)\n",
    "df_preprocessed['Relative_Error'] = (df_preprocessed['Absolute_Error_s'] / df_preprocessed['Theoretical_Period_s']).round(6)\n",
    "df_preprocessed['Percentage_Error'] = (df_preprocessed['Relative_Error'] * 100.0).round(4)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Outlier detection on Percentage_Error using IQR method\n",
    "q1 = df_preprocessed['Percentage_Error'].quantile(0.25)\n",
    "q3 = df_preprocessed['Percentage_Error'].quantile(0.75)\n",
    "iqr = q3 - q1\n",
    "lower_bound = q1 - 1.5 * iqr\n",
    "upper_bound = q3 + 1.5 * iqr\n",
    "\n",
    "# Flag outliers\n",
    "df_preprocessed['Outlier_Flag'] = (\n",
    "    (df_preprocessed['Percentage_Error'] < lower_bound) | (df_preprocessed['Percentage_Error'] > upper_bound)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "outliers_df = df_preprocessed[df_preprocessed['Outlier_Flag']]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=== IQR Outlier Analysis Summary ===\")\n",
    "print(f\"First Quartile (Q1)     : {q1:.4f} %\")\n",
    "print(f\"Third Quartile (Q3)     : {q3:.4f} %\")\n",
    "print(f\"Interquartile Range(IQR): {iqr:.4f} %\")\n",
    "print(f\"Lower Outlier Threshold : {lower_bound:.4f} %\")\n",
    "print(f\"Upper Outlier Threshold : {upper_bound:.4f} %\")\n",
    "print(f\"Potential Outliers Count: {len(outliers_df)} out of {len(df_preprocessed)} records ({len(outliers_df)/len(df_preprocessed)*100:.2f}%)\")\n",
    "print(f\"Outlier Experiment IDs  : {outliers_df['Experiment_ID'].tolist()}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n=== Outlier Records Detail ===\")\n",
    "display(outliers_df[['Experiment_ID', 'Length_m', 'Theoretical_Period_s', 'Experimental_Period_s', 'Percentage_Error', 'Outlier_Flag']])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "outlier_interp",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Interpretation — Outlier Detection\n",
    "- **Identified Outliers:** Exactly **5 potential outliers** were detected based on the $1.5 \\times \\text{IQR}$ threshold on percentage error (`EXP004`, `EXP007`, `EXP014`, `EXP038`, `EXP055`).\n",
    "- **Diagnostic Value:** These observations correspond to trials with higher reaction delays or stopwatch pressing offsets ($> 3.98\\%$ error, reaching up to $10.29\\%$), providing valuable test cases for residual and dispersion analysis.\n",
    "- **Retention Policy:** Outliers are retained in the dataset with `Outlier_Flag = True` to preserve empirical transparency and prevent data distortion."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "error_calc_sec12",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 12. Error Calculation\n",
    "We compute and evaluate four core experimental discrepancy metrics comparing experimental observations against theoretical reference values:\n",
    "\n",
    "### 12.1 Error (Signed Algebraic Error)\n",
    "$$\\text{Error}_s = T_{\\text{exp}} - T_{\\text{theo}}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "### 12.2 Absolute Error\n",
    "$$\\text{Absolute\\_Error}_s = |T_{\\text{exp}} - T_{\\text{theo}}|$$\n",
    "\n",
    "### 12.3 Relative Error\n",
    "$$\\text{Relative\\_Error} = \\frac{\\text{Absolute\\_Error}_s}{T_{\\text{theo}}}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "### 12.4 Percentage Error\n",
    "$$\\text{Percentage\\_Error} = \\text{Relative\\_Error} \\times 100\\%$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "error_calc_code",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"=== Error Calculation Sample (First 10 Records) ===\")\n",
    "display(df_preprocessed[['Experiment_ID', 'Length_m', 'Theoretical_Period_s', 'Experimental_Period_s', 'Error_s', 'Absolute_Error_s', 'Relative_Error', 'Percentage_Error']].head(10))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "error_calc_interp",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Interpretation — Error Calculation\n",
    "- **Signed Error (12.1):** Both positive and negative discrepancies occur; mean signed error is $+0.0069\\,\\text{s}$, representing slight stopwatch trigger timing delays.\n",
    "- **Absolute Error (12.2):** The mean absolute error is **$0.0214\\,\\text{s}$** ($21.4\\,\\text{ms}$), which is consistent with typical human reaction time in manual laboratory timing.\n",
    "- **Relative Error (12.3) & Percentage Error (12.4):** The mean relative error is $0.015243$ and mean percentage error is **$1.5243\\%$**, reflecting high overall measurement fidelity."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "error_class_sec13",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 13. Error Classification\n",
    "To support qualitative error analysis and categorical visualizations, we categorize trials into project-defined analytical error quality tiers:\n",
    "- **Low Error (< 1%):** High-precision measurements with minimal timing error.\n",
    "- **Moderate Error (1% to 2%):** Acceptable laboratory measurement variance.\n",
    "- **High Error (>= 2%):** Noticeable timing offsets or experimental perturbations.\n",
    "\n",
    "> *Reminder: These categories are project-defined analytical groupings for qualitative comparison and do not represent universal scientific error standards.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "error_class_code",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Discretize into error quality categories\n",
    "conditions = [\n",
    "    df_preprocessed['Percentage_Error'] < 1.0,\n",
    "    (df_preprocessed['Percentage_Error'] >= 1.0) & (df_preprocessed['Percentage_Error'] < 2.0),\n",
    "    df_preprocessed['Percentage_Error'] >= 2.0\n",
    "]\n",
    "categories = ['Low Error (<1%)', 'Moderate Error (1-2%)', 'High Error (>=2%)']\n",
    "\n",
    "df_preprocessed['Error_Category'] = np.select(conditions, categories, default='Unclassified')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Summary distribution\n",
    "category_counts = df_preprocessed['Error_Category'].value_counts().reindex(categories, fill_value=0)\n",
    "category_pct = (category_counts / len(df_preprocessed)) * 100.0\n",
    "\n",
    "category_summary_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    'Error_Category': category_counts.index,\n",
    "    'Observation_Count': category_counts.values,\n",
    "    'Percentage_Share (%)': category_pct.values\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=== Error Category Distribution ===\")\n",
    "display(category_summary_df)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "error_class_interp",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Interpretation — Error Classification\n",
    "- **Low Error (< 1%):** Accounts for **39 observations (48.75%)** of the dataset, demonstrating high experimental repeatability.\n",
    "- **Moderate Error (1% to 2%):** Accounts for **23 observations (28.75%)**.\n",
