    "## 18. Important Findings\n",
    "\n",
    "Based on quantitative analysis of the simple pendulum experimental dataset ($N = 80$), seven key findings are established:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **High Model Agreement ($r = +0.992$):**  \n",
    "   Empirical oscillation periods strongly conform to the theoretical simple pendulum model $T = 2\\pi\\sqrt{L/g}$ across all 8 lengths ($0.20\\,\\text{m}$ to $1.00\\,\\text{m}$), exhibiting a near-perfect Pearson correlation of $r = +0.992$.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. **Human-Scale Timing Accuracy ($\text{MAE} = 0.0214\,\text{s}$):**  \n",
    "   The overall mean absolute timing error is $0.0214\\,\\text{s}$ ($21.4\\,\\text{ms}$) with a dataset mean percentage error of $1.5243\\%$, which aligns with expected human visual-auditory stopwatch reaction latencies ($20 - 40\\,\\text{ms}$).\n",
    "\n",
    "3. **Dominance of High-Precision Observations ($77.50\%$ Sub-2%):**  \n",
    "   Nearly half of all observations (**$48.75\\%$**, 39 trials) exhibit less than $1.0\\%$ error, and **$77.50\\%$** (62 trials) fall below the sub-$2.0\\%$ error boundary, demonstrating high experimental repeatability.\n",
    "\n",
    "4. **Length-Invariant Error Behavior ($r = -0.123$):**  \n",
    "   The Pearson correlation between pendulum length and percentage error is negligible ($r = -0.123$), proving that relative timing error is scale-invariant and does not accumulate systematically as pendulum length increases.\n",
    "   \n",
    "5. **Effective Outlier Isolation ($6.25\%$ Anomaly Rate):**  \n",
    "   The Interquartile Range method ($1.5 \\times \\text{IQR}$) isolated exactly 5 statistical anomalies ($> 3.9822\\%$ error), with the single maximum discrepancy reaching $10.2896\\%$ in trial `EXP055` ($L = 0.70\\,\\text{m}$).\n",
    "\n",
    "6. **Right-Skewed Residual Distribution:**  \n",
    "   The percentage error distribution displays pronounced positive skewness, with the median error ($1.0119\\%$) notably lower than the mean ($1.5243\\%$), confirming that large measurement discrepancies are rare, isolated events.\n",
    "\n",
    "7. **Length Extreme Performance:**  \n",
    "   The lowest mean percentage error occurred at length $0.80\\,\\text{m}$ ($0.9080\\%$, highest precision), whereas the highest mean percentage error occurred at length $0.50\\,\\text{m}$ ($2.1026\\%$, driven by negative outlier `EXP038`)."
